# Audio fixtures are BINARY, said out loud.
#
# Git already detects this correctly (m4a is full of NUL bytes, and `git diff --numstat` reports
# `-` for them), so this file changes no behaviour today. It exists because the cost of being
# wrong is asymmetric: tests\assets\recordings holds the ONLY speech this project has, it is what
# `tools\transcribe.ps1` scores the engine against, and a fixture silently mangled by newline
# normalisation would not fail loudly -- it would decode to noise and read as "the engine got
# worse", which is the exact misdiagnosis docs\VOICE-ENGINE-PLAN.md was written to prevent.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT `* text=auto`. This repo has already paid for line-ending confusion once
# (VOICE-INPUT-PLAN.md D-V10: a working copy with 869 CRLF and 108 bare LF lines, invisible to
# `git diff` because git normalises what it is handed, and red on one machine while green on
# another). A repo-wide normalisation rule introduced casually is how that bill gets paid twice.
# These two lines match nothing but audio.
*.m4a binary
*.wav binary
